---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us & Our Testing Methodology"
  description="Learn how Productivity Software Reviews tests, benchmarks, and evaluates SaaS tools for small business owners and creators."
>
  <div class="prose-container">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="badge">About the Publication</span>
      <h1>Software Reviews Written for Builders, Not Enterprise IT Buyers</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">
        We help small business owners, agencies, and independent creators choose reliable software without drowning in bloated feature matrices.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="prose-section">
      <h2>Why We Started Productivity Software Reviews</h2>
      <p>
        If you run a 5-person agency, a solo consulting practice, or a growing creator business, buying software has become unnecessarily exhausting. Most review websites either copy-paste vendor marketing bullet points or evaluate tools from the perspective of a 500-person corporate IT department.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Productivity Software Reviews</strong> was built to fix that gap. We focus exclusively on how modern SaaS tools perform for lean, fast-moving teams where every subscription dollar and every hour of onboarding time counts.
      </p>

      <h2>Our 4-Step Hands-On Testing Process</h2>
      <p>
        We never publish a review based solely on a vendor press release or a 5-minute free-trial walkthrough. Every product we benchmark goes through four stages:
      </p>

      <div class="method-grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>1. Real Workflow Migration</h3>
          <p>
            We load realistic project data—client deliverables, recurring weekly tasks, SOP documents, and contractor permissions—into every tool we test.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>2. True Cost Calculation</h3>
          <p>
            We calculate what a 1-person, 5-person, and 15-person business will actually pay per year, calling out seat minimums, paid add-ons, and guest limits.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>3. Daily Friction Audit</h3>
          <p>
            We measure app speed, mobile usability, keyboard shortcuts, and how easy it is for non-technical teammates or clients to collaborate.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>4. Clear "Best For" Verdicts</h3>
          <p>
            No single tool is right for everyone. We tell you plainly who should buy a tool—and who should skip it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Editorial Independence</h2>
      <p>
        Our editorial team operates independently from our business partnerships. Software vendors cannot pay to be included in our roundups, cannot pay to raise their numerical rating, and never get to preview or edit our reviews before publication. For full details on how we fund our testing, please read our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">Affiliate Disclosure</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header h1 {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }

  .method-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 2.25rem;
  }

  .method-grid h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .method-grid p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .method-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
